data.content:
Your code **does not use `Thread.Abort`** (or `Thread.Interrupt`, `ThreadAbortException`, or `Thread.ResetAbort`). It only uses:

- `Thread.Start()` 
- `Thread.Join()`
- `Thread.Sleep()`

These APIs all work identically in .NET 8 — **no migration is needed** for this code.

That said, you could modernize it to use `Task`/`Parallel` for cleaner async patterns:

```csharp
public class SimpleWorker
{
    public void RunBatch(List<WorkItem> items)
    {
        Parallel.ForEach(items, item => Process(item));
    }

    private void Process(WorkItem item)
    {
        Thread.Sleep(100);
        item.Result = ComputeResult(item.Input);
    }
}
```

